  "notes": "Inventory is the complete developer-facing surface this feature exposes in dedicated workers per the current specification: the exposure change itself, the Document Policy gating (js-profiling-mode enum with eager/lazy, deprecated js-profiling boolean), the Profiler interface members (constructor, sampleInterval, stopped, stop(), samplebufferfull), and the five trace/init dictionaries plus the ProfilerResource typedef (documented with ProfilerTrace). The spec defines NO sample() method — on-demand sampling exists only as the Force Sample WebDriver extension command, noted on the child page. Chrome's trial exposes the interface in DedicatedWorkerGlobalScope only (ProfilerAPIForDedicatedWorker) although the spec IDL says Worker; the pages state both. The chromestatus dev-trial milestone moved to 154 after this v147 page was published; the route and identity are stable per the durable contract and the overview carries an honest milestone note. DOMHighResTimeStamp and EventTarget are external platform types, not feature surface."
}
